This search input calls the backend on every keystroke and doesn't cancel stale requests:

```jsx
function Search() {
  const [results, setResults] = useState([]);
  function onChange(e) {
    fetchSearch(e.target.value).then(setResults);
  }
  return <input onChange={onChange} />;
}
```

This function fetches details for a list of order IDs by calling the upstream API once per ID in a loop:

```js
async function getOrderDetails(orderIds) {
  const results = [];
  for (const id of orderIds) {
    results.push(await fetchOrder(id));
  }
  return results;
}
```

The upstream API has a batch endpoint: POST /orders/batch with a list of IDs.
